<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Greatest volume of an open box</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Equal squares of side \(x\) cm are cut from the corners of a square sheet of [[if test="is(s0<=48)"]]manila paper[[else]]galvanised iron[[/if]] \({@s0@}\) cm by \({@s0@}\) cm, and the sides are folded up to make an open box.</p><p>(a) Write the volume \(V\) cm\(^3\) in terms of \(x\).</p><div>\(V =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Find the value of \(x\) that gives the greatest volume.</p><div>\(x =\) [[input:ans2]] cm [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>(c) Find the greatest volume.</p><div>[[input:ans3]] cm\(^3\) [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) Cutting a square from each corner shortens each edge of the base at both ends, so the base is \({@s0-2*x@}\) cm square and the height is \(x\) cm:</p><p>\[V = {@Vm@} = {@expand(Vm)@}, \qquad 0 \lt x \lt {@x2@}\]</p><p>(b) \(\dfrac{dV}{dx} = {@diff(expand(Vm),x)@} = {@(6*x-s0)*(2*x-s0)@}\), which is \(0\) when \(x = {@xb@}\) or \(x = {@x2@}\). At \(x = {@x2@}\) the base has side \(0\), so there is no box. \(\dfrac{d^2V}{dx^2} = {@diff(expand(Vm),x,2)@}\), which is \({@-4*s0@}\) at \(x = {@xb@}\): negative, so this gives the greatest volume.</p><p>(c) The box is \({@bs@}\) cm by \({@bs@}\) cm by \({@xb@}\) cm, and \(V = [[if test="is(Vb>=10000)"]]{#floor(Vb/1000)#}\,{#floor(mod(Vb,1000)/100)#}{#floor(mod(Vb,100)/10)#}{#mod(Vb,10)#}[[else]]{#Vb#}[[/if]]\) cm\(^3\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[validate_x(ex) := if every(lambda([v], member(v, [x])), listofvars(ex)) then "" else "Use x as the only letter in your answer.";
/* Design: open box from a square sheet, with a randomised side. Source: adapted from SMP AS/A2 Core 1, chapter 9, Exercise D question 5. */
ix: 1+rand(10);
s0: [12,18,24,30,36,42,48,54,60,66][ix];
Vm: x*(s0-2*x)^2;
xb: s0/6; Vb: 2*s0^3/27; bs: s0-2*xb;
Vone: x*(s0-x)^2; Vsq: x^2*(s0-2*x);
x2: s0/2; x3: s0/3;
Vbad: 25*s0^3/216; Vone3: 4*s0^3/27;]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
