  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Differentiation II: greatest volume of an open box</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 4.1: Model the volume of an open box folded from a square sheet, and find the best cut and the greatest volume.</p><p id="edition">Core</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Question 5 in Exercise D of Chapter 9 of Cassell, D., Instone, S., Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP AS/A2 Mathematics: Core 1 for AQA, Cambridge University Press, 2004: a square sheet with a randomised side, Kenyan materials and diagnostic feedback.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
